# docs/adaptive-layout-plan.md §2. The subject stays `row@dash` through
# both states: identity is the creation kind, presentation is the prop.
expect label#0 "alpha"
expect_axis row@dash "horizontal"
expect_axis column@steady "vertical"
click button#0
expect_axis row@dash "vertical"
click button#0
expect_axis row@dash "horizontal"
# THE BREAKPOINT HALF (docs/adaptive-layout-plan.md D3): iOS reports the
# platform's own size class, every other platform derives compact below
# 600 points. Every assert sits AFTER a resize because the initial state
# is width-dependent (the panes-band rule); the phone lanes cut at
# resize_window and assert their always-narrow truth as an extra step
# (the MODS tables in tools/lib/lanes/{ios,android}.py).
resize_window 480x400
expect_axis row@narrow "vertical"
# The grid's columns follow the class too (D6.2, ruled 2026-09-05).
expect_grid_columns grid@sheet 1
# Crossing back AUTO-REVERTS: the diff-against-base rule, so there is no
# second declaration anywhere.
resize_window 900x600
expect_axis row@narrow "horizontal"
expect_grid_columns grid@sheet 3
